o polished interior and  electric polishing offers a number of  benefits what electro polishing does is  it removes the surface roughness and  microscopic structure on stainless steel  and by smoothing and removing some of  that microscopic structure what that  means is that it significantly reduces  microscopic areas where microorganisms  could attach  and it improves the corrosion resistance  and eases cleaning  now many of you are using sterilization  by vaporized hydrogen peroxide in your  clean room  and that's we're seeing that a lot so we  wanted to make sure that our incubator  was compatible with these processes  i will say that a lot of companies are  offering vhp now and not all of them are  the same some of them are using  chemicals in addition to hydrogen  peroxide such as per acetic acid  and those additional chemicals can  exacerbate  pitting and corrosion  by the chemical  so  i will say that we've looked really  exclusively at the steris procedure  because  the moisture is controlled  so when you have the vapor condense  because the humidity is not controlled  that increases the dwell time of that  hydrogen peroxide and that can result  over time in again damage to the  stainless steel so we do recommend only  the steris dry non-condensing vhp  process  another part of that is that any company  that's offering this should  should offer you tests to confirm  that the process actually worked that  you have complete elimination complete  sterilization  so complete and elimination of those  microorganisms that are removed by  sterilization and finally it's important  that that vapor that gas be neutralized  and proven neutralized because hydrogen  peroxide in high concentrations  is toxic to humans and it is a known  carcinogen so that's why these  procedures are performed by trained  technicians wearing  protective personal equipment  so not everybody is using vhp processes  so this incubator also includes  an automated high temperature  sterilization 