h because i talked about this a year  ago and you can find that talk online  but temperature recovery is very  different depending on the design of the  incubator different technologies produce  very different conditions and so as you  see the fastest recovery back to 37  degrees following a 30 second door  opening is provided by active air flow  circulation in the chamber  carbon dioxide is the second biggest  parameter provided by the incubator and  so i want to review i think many of us  don't really think about  why we provide co2 we know it's required  for cell growth and we know it's there  to balance the ph of the growth medium  but this system is actually based on the  physiological  conditions in the bloodstream and the  lung  so as this is my drawing of a blood  vessel entering a lobe of a lung and so  you see that every cell in the body is  putting out carbon dioxide as a waste  by-product of metabolism  such that the oxygen concentration in  the lungs is pretty high it's five  percent co2 that's different than the  air that we breathe which is currently  about 0.04 percent co2 so to mimic that  physiological concentration we provide  five percent co2 in the incubator most  commonly it really depends a little bit  on what what you're using for growth  medium and i'll talk about that in just  a minute  oxygen in the lungs is about 14 percent  i don't have time today to talk about  physiological oxygen  but i do want to point out that also in  the bloodstream there's a natural buffer  of bicarbonate ions and if you look at  that concentration it's equal to about  two milligrams per milliliter of sodium  bicarbonate which is the most common  buffer used in cell growth media  so if we look at that biochemistry a  little bit the buffer in the growth  medium the sodium bicarbonate works with  that co2 gas  the buffer takes up and gives off  protons to balance the ph keeping at a  physiological neutral ph of 7.4  now fluctuations in the co2  concentration can affect the morphology  and growth of your cells  if the co2 concentration is too high or  too low you'll see changes in your cells  that are reflective of toxicity because  the ph is either too acidic or too basic  so the control of the co2 is critical  and the co2 recovery to the set  conditions of five percent the most  commonly used concentration  varies very differently depending on the  different technologies included in that  incubator and again i'm not going to go  through this table because i've done it  elsewhere but just to point out that  even different sensors  that are precision can work differently  depending on the incubator design and  what's the airflow like in that  incubator  finally humidity we provide high  humidity in the incubator to reduce  evaporation from the growth media  because in low humidity water is the  only thing that evaporates from culture  media and as a result the remaining  salts minerals hormones in the growth  media become concentrated such that  toxic conditions can result so just like  too much salt in your diet is bad for  you  maybe some minerals and your vitamins  are you know if you take too many uh  multivitamins per day that can result in  toxic concentrations  that is also true  for the cells  which are derived from our tissues and  evaporation is four times faster at 80  percent humidity than at 93 percent  humidity and greater  so it's important to have high humidity  to prevent evaporation but too much  humidity is also bad so humidity higher  than about 95 approaches 100 humidity  and 100 humidity of course is rain or  fog so when the humidity is too high  that can result in condensation of that  moisture into liquid droplets or even  puddles in your incubator and that  condensation can provide a great  breeding ground for microorganisms  so proper control of humidity is  critical for healthy cells  and just like temperature and  co2 humidity recovery varies greatly  depending on the design of the incubator  and different technologies produce very  different conditions  so we like to provide a protected  integrated reservoir  for the humidity in the hair cell biocr  co2 incubator which provides  good balance but fast humidity recovery  in a dry condensation free chamber  to help provide good cell growth  but it's also very controlled and i i  know that in a lot of clean rooms  an open reservoir of water like a water  pan is frowned upon so in this incubator  the water reservoir is completely  covered and protected  the hepa filter helps to pull  contamination away from the water  finally in-chamber sensors are encrypt  are critical for proper recovery  and  accuracy of the of the temperature co2  and humidity in your cells in chamber  sensors experience the same conditions  as yourselves if you open the door you  want the sensor to react without that  condition just like your cells would  react they continuously sample and react  and adjust the conditions so that your  cells are in their ideal conditions as  much as possible and they provide better  recovery now that may seem pretty  pretty  expected for an incubator but i will  tell you that not every incubator  includes sensors in the chamber they  might be present in in a design where  samples of air from the chamber are  removed and passed to the sensor outside  the incubator chamber  uniformity throughout the chamber i've  talked about this a few times why is  this important without good uniformity  that means that cells in different areas  experience different conditions so if  you are have some cultured vessels in  the top left or some in the bottom right  of the incubator  and they there isn't good uniformity  then that can result in variability in  your results and some cells may never  experience the proper conditions  such that in the end your cell therapy  doesn't meet your quality and  characteristic analysis that is required  so  i know we think about this maybe with  temperature but i also want to point out  yo